    <Placemark>
      <name>Hakarlavogur</name>
      <description><![CDATA[Hot Spring is situated on private property. Bathing is only allowed with the owner's permission. Hákarlavogur geothermal pool, despite its secluded location, has gained widespread recognition as one of Iceland's most famous hot pools. Its claim to fame stems from a memorable photo shoot featuring Jason Momoa, renowned for his role as Khal Drogo in the popular TV series Game of Thrones, which took place at this very pool. Finding Hákarlavogur can be quite a challenge. Tucked away among the rocks along the Atlantic shore, it remains hidden behind the airport, adding an element of mystery to its allure.
