    <Placemark>
      <name>Emstrur</name>
      <description><![CDATA[https://nat.is/emstrur-plains/ Emstrur is a desolate grazing area in the southern interior, northwest of the icecap Myrdalsjokull. A few free standing low and steep mountains decorate the area through which the so-called "Laugavegur" hiking trail between Landmannalaugar and Thorsmork lies. In Gully Hattfellsgil is a mountain station of the farmers, who round up the sheep after the summer grazings. .
