    <Placemark>
      <name>Hótel Laugarhóll Swimming pool</name>
      <description><![CDATA[https://goo.gl/maps/fePYiCLzLfHjT7iA6 Opening hours: The swimming pool is open all year from 8:00 to 22:00. Info: Next to the hotel you will find The Pool of Gvendur the Good, a geothermal outdoor swimming pool (35°C) and adjacent natural thermal spring (41°C), perfect to relax in after a long day on the road or hiking in the wilderness. This pool was built by the farmers and is owned by the whole community and there for does not belong to hotel guests only. The big pool is emptied and cleaned every Tuesday but the natural warm pools remain open every day. ATTENTION! There is no lifeguard at the pool. Please be careful and never let your children out of sight! CAREFUL! The natural pool can be slippery. Price: - 500 ISK/adult - 250 ISK/children 6-12 years old - Free for children 0-5 years old Credit cards accepted at the hotel reception from May 1st to September 30th.
