    <Placemark>
      <name>Ólafsfjörður Swimming Pool</name>
      <description><![CDATA[https://sundlaugar.is/en/sundlaugasafn/olafsfjordur-swimming-pool/ Opening hours: Summer opening (11th June until 31st August): Mondays – Fridays: 06:30 – 19:00 Weekends: 10:00 – 18:00 Winter opening. Mondays: 06:30 – 19:00 Tuesdays: 06:30 – 08:00 and 09:00 – 19:00 Wednesdays: 06:30 – 08:00 and 14:30 – 19:00 Thursdays: 06:30 – 19:00 Fridays: 06:30 – 08:00 and 14:30 – 19:00 Saturdays: 10:00 – 14:00 Sundays: 14:00 – 18:00 The swimming pool in Ólafsfjörður is 8 x 25 meters. There are two hot tubs, one is 38°C and the other is 40°C. One is a Jacuzzi. There are two water slides that are very popular, one is a snake that is 3,5 meters and the other is a black hole. The swimming pool was built by volunteers in the sports club between 1943 – 1945. In 2010 the area was renovated. Price: - 700 ISK/adult - 330 ISK/children 10-15 years old - Free for children 0-9 years old
