    <Placemark>
      <name>Hveragerði Swimming Pool</name>
      <description><![CDATA[https://sundlaugar.is/en/frettir/sundlaugin-i-hveragerdi-lokar/ Opening hours: Summer opening (15. May to 15. August): Weekdays: 06:45 – 21:00 Weekends: 10:00 – 19:00 Winter opening (16. August to 14. May): Mondays to Thursdays: 06:45 – 20:15 Fridays: 06:45 – 17:15 Weekends: 10:00 – 17:15 The swimming pool was built by volunteers and opened in 1938. For a while it was the biggest swimming pool in Iceland and the Icelandic national team used it for practising until Laugardalslaug in Reykjavík was opened. Originally the pool was 25 meters long but is now 50 meters long and 12 meters wide. The water in the pool is heated with the geothermal heat and that ensures the normal acid level and purity of the water. The pool has a warm hand shallow children's pool and a Jacuzzi. There is also a natural steam bath. The pool is located in a beautiful surrounding with a good shelter. There is always a staff on duty and also a CCTV system to keep the guests as safe as possible. Price: - 900 ISK/adult - 350 ISK/children 6-17 years old - Free for children 0-5 years old
https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AKcrxGTZBalrAphKflsuF07WmLzebWGq-Iw9C9nHBKUfI3pOprnvEPSRv3DokZxs88En67wREJG5k5Jh3o5SVvctNpugZ6oYleSvyjPRm_WfJ1FmGO8lz42exF41wQ0iw6126ZDUBVQMBvtUn1UT8SmnpeGPNM0UVnUYtMNFol_9G8ZYk1Vq13t3ta82aa6oJ68a_UEhR5qHULmnDInckHNRfguNTSCsYE4R2kLXCGItYoiWueLfZgnFNpdUwGs?authuser=0&fife=s16383
