    <Placemark>
      <name>Westman Islands Swimming pool</name>
      <description><![CDATA[https://sundlaugar.is/en/sundlaugasafn/vestmannaeyjar-2/ Opening hours: Summer opening (1. June to the middle of August): Weekdays: 6:15 – 21:00 Weekends: 09:00 – 18:00 Winter opening (from the middle of August to 31. May): Weekdays: 06:15 until 14:00 (indoor pool used by schools) – 21:00 Weekends: 09:00 – 17:00 The swimming pool in the Westman islands was first opened in 1976. In 2008 was started to build a new outdoor part of the swimming pool and it was opened in 2010 and is considered among the best in Iceland. The indoor swimming pool is 25 x 11 meters with 0,9% salted water. The pool has a 1 meter high spring board, floating equipment and more to entertain the children. The outdoor area has two hot tubs and one large Jacuzzi. From the Jacuzzi it is easy for the parents to watch their children anywhere in the area. There is a large children´s pool with a climbing wall, basket hoops, children´s water slider and an area for the youngest. There are also two water sliders. One has a trampoline in it where the users bounce off into the water. The area also has a large sunbathing area. The area is monitored with 12 security cameras. During weekends the temperature is increased from 29,5°C to 31,5°C. Price: - 900 ISK/adult - 200 ISK/children 10-17 years old - Free for children 0-9 years old
https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AKcrxGS3fgoLgn1eZbyEXRvln0f9rjl6GIniGW2rh_cSFLOdUacXHC9F_55mA-OTNTtsWX36fi8KZJ3M-V5a8BdS3g2VWYByxZdgp1nI02DlPBI0X9tf6HrhhLpJE_wJiGC0Deip2b25uRogc38RCxLIhdk7BbuCwdeuBSDUsjHE1V-MW781pPLhPcaXOT-9gfLjINCBjZPU2bWyIPMGX1kC6Ji0YkuBQVY1ZhMdz6xCGF8gT-_Y7wujrE2wdwY?authuser=0&fife=s16383
