    <Placemark>
      <name>Hveragerði Campsite</name>
      <description><![CDATA[https://tjalda.is/en/hveragerdi/ Hveragerdi is a small village about 30 minutes away from Reykjavik. It is known for its geothermal activity and the Reykjadalur hike, with its "hot river" is a popular attraction. The campsite is located in a peaceful environment and since it's in a town, you have everything you need close by, including stores, a swimming pool, playgrounds, and even a golf course. It has a nice service house where you can wash your clothes and dishes. Open: All year around Book online: https://parka.is/hveragerdi/ Phone: 857-9903 Price: ISK 1,750/adult. Free for 0-15 year old children. Facilities: - WC - Shower - Electricity (ISK 1000) - Water - Cooking facilities - Hiking trails - Washer/dryer (ISK 800 each) - Playground - Horse rental - Store access - Pool/hot tub - Wi-Fi - Waste disposal - Horse rental - Dogs allowed
