    </Placemark>
    <Placemark>
      <name>Þingeyraroddi Camping Ground</name>
      <description><![CDATA[https://tjalda.is/en/thingeyraroddi/ Please note that during wintertime frosts, water is not available. You will have to use swimming pool facilities. The swimming pool is open 8-10 in the morning and 4-6 in the afternoon (closed on Saturdays and open 10-4 on Sundays) Þingeyri is a small town with a rich history. The inhabitants of Þingeyri have built up a Viking-based tourism, with a Viking ship that sails with travelers on the sea and Viking festivals that are held where Vikings fight each other while they are not serving the guests. The town has a swimming pool, beach volleyball area and a few restaurants. The surroundings from Þingeyri offer a wide variety for horseback riding or hiking. The campsite is right by the local swimming pool, where you will have access to showers and bathrooms. However, during the wintertime, you will not have access to the campsite service building, where summer visitors have access to electricity, water, etc. Phone: 450-8470 Price: ISK 1,830 Facilities: - Electricity (1200 ISK) - Water (Swimming pool only in winter) - Shower (Swimming pool only in winter) - Playground - WC (Swimming pool only in winter) - Washing machine - Dryer
https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AKcrxGQErPf-Qk1xIVFSNwwoIE8zSSiLTn-eWEBNHO5iE5fWWNO-SOGoVyoyOAQKAAwcYgTbPX0WnYQ0tq1XFbmASeGj6bT5F_nq2GWXLFHM5kejPBQtDC134ltcyRDoiDN7alTCahWJ7kegE3GNFCECGbKphMz3ovYmY1yHQPdWoain2aPETYFjoZVtD0JE_90iAHgNTlLfWvHkI1lg3TGZfnE6fix5fcBbxE7wgJ1qMZfMmToOHfK0_57vF5M?authuser=0&fife=s16383
https://tjalda.is/en/thingeyraroddi/

