      <styleUrl>#style_Campsites___Mountain_Huts</styleUrl>
      <Point>
        <coordinates>-21.567584,64.311957,0.0</coordinates>
      </Point>
    </Placemark>
    <Placemark>
      <name>Hotel Reykjanes Campsite</name>
      <description><![CDATA[https://goo.gl/maps/HihNuhDY9XqrPezp6 This campsite is located by Hotel Reykjanes. All the facilities for the Campsite are run and closely linked to the hotel so they are in accordance with hotel standards. The restaurant is open to all guests as well as the snack bar. The showers are open to all camping guests as well as the geothermal swimming pool that is one of a kind, along with the old green sauna and hot tubs. On goods days you can swim in the sea and on almost any given day you can walk a short distance to experience some amazing nature and wildlife (such as seals if you're lucky) Reykjanes has a lot of geothermal energy and all buildings are heated by the local springs. Local swimming pool is 50 x 12.5 meters and is located below the hotel. The pool is also heated by self-running hot geothermal water. Surrounding most of the pool is a fence. There is also a sun-platform and steambath aside the pool along with extremely popular benches to sit on underneath the water. Dressing rooms are right next to the pool with good showers. The swimming pool is always warm and because of that, many travelers that visit Reykjanes, say that it is one of the most effective resting places in the Westfjords, because the fatigue and stress will disappear in the hot water and clean air. Phone: +354 456 4844 Price: Kr. 2900/camper Facilities: - WC - Showers - Water - Pool/hot tub - Restaurant - Sauna - Hiking paths - Electricity (Kr. 1000)
https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AKcrxGSWjRe-BkZ2dwT3k9FP9TRiMzaeDSnIw7Pcu1PyZZHqMNw6sG42EwG33x4Wa3e1e00F9DGL3kJSyyGAHy7jECmks54ScX2Bph68vivs0_jN_T-aIOpFSBMcEg1viViM5Yx3L0kB2_fYeSW_tlVO6P_UtTGU7EoYjtIQOuH9BOPR2899e4AgxIbLVGbCPQiT67tbggkwkYDTHgVo4hLyxCyDKIqs0uzjKTq6CXEx49UnA4saT-bWjSGXV-0?authuser=0&fife=s16383
https://goo.gl/maps/HihNuhDY9XqrPezp6

