    </Placemark>
    <Placemark>
      <name>Hólar Campsite</name>
      <description><![CDATA[https://tjalda.is/en/holar/ Hólar in the valley Hjaltadalur is one of the more historic sites in Iceland and a popular tourist attraction. The history, sanctity and the natural beauty all work together to attract people to Hólar. In the forest there are many small areas the provide good shelter for tents and mobile homes. There are many walking paths in the area as well as a restaurant and a swimming pool. The camp site has toilet facilities with hot and cold running water. There is not electricity in the camp site but that is one of the factors that makes this camp site the charming camp site it is. The camp sites in the town Sauðárkrókur, Hofsós, Varmahlíð and at Hólar are operated together. It is possible to stay the first night in one of these camp sites and pay less during the next night in some of the other camp sites. It is necessary to provide a receipt from the first camp site. The camp site is open from the 15th of May until the 16th of September sooner or later as the weather allows. Phone: +354 899 3231 Price: 1500 ISK Per person first day 1300 ISK Per person every additional night 1300 ISK Per pensioner(age 67+) first day 1100 ISK Per pensioner every additional night Children 12 years and younger Free of charge Facilities: - WC - Water - Playground - Hiking paths - Pool/hot tub - Dogs allowed
https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AKcrxGQSxo0unSzgBqg8yGA0k57_dXYmdg7amGaFAfKwGS8sae0nuyVIJx0bMfIKpqYR32YiFKHGiciGqFf4uBxwvASzTILgTzngwfiNrfIP6dSgC29Y1NGbO2K92aTKTVB4D8wBwJv9RIEAQrVV2c68a9btvHfwod_ypBUA-PS5zcmtTMYg2IFGuFAgg_IJjUMFbK_s38oFY_xsa8VZgmvjgdOqHo-PPF0rZbpglEKWLJoCZn1wWs_Iy9Qbesw?authuser=0&fife=s16383
https://tjalda.is/en/holar/

