    </Placemark>
    <Placemark>
      <name>Ásbyrgi Campsite</name>
      <description><![CDATA[https://tjalda.is/en/asbyrgi/ The national park is open to guests all year round. It has a big camp site for tents, folding campers and mobile homes. In the western valley (Vesturdal) there is a beautiful camp site with less service, it is open from 10th of june to the 15th of september. The camp site in Ásbyrgi is open from 15th of may to the 15th of september. There is a large camp site in Ásbyrgi for tents, camping folders and mobile homes. In the service house there are 4 showers for men and 4 for women. You can also find there washing machine and a tumble dryer. In Ásbyrgi there is also the visitor center, Gljúfrastofa. There you can find information and also a display on Ásbyrgi and Jökulsárgljúfur. It is open daily from the 1st of may to the 31st of october. The store at Ásbyrgi is open daily from 09 – 22 during the summer time. It is also a restaurant. There are many great walking paths in Ásbyrgi. During the summer there are also educational trips, evening walks, camp fire during the first weekend in august and much more. The campsite in Ásbyrgi is open from mid-May until the end of October each year. Opening date is subject to snowfall in winter and snow melt in spring. Book online: https://parka.is/asbyrgi/ Phone: +354 470 7100 Price: Kr. 1500/adult - Kr. 700/13-16 yr. old - Free for 12 and younger Facilities: - WC - Water - Shower (Kr. 300) - Washer/dryer (Kr. 500/500) - Electricity (Kr. 1000) - Walking paths - Golf course - Playground - WiFi - Waste disposal - Dogs allowed https://www.youtube.com/embed/Rsv940aSL4I
https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AKcrxGRITwweKaBjnXfYHt04AaHMpu8Vj1PZ8-nWzW5jOV8sx33ncTavAhAPyaJqRQlRaBatOVY72hHJg7SkPf-DCvYDBNy8UhRX2dV5XmSOfqM2vqPnAsSFBSeiycE79xVe5DH8wvyVPG3Bg8oSrJBDMxjCqrEGRC9FEk-IM3iTbAN37NFTfm2c8CzIDLQQMVdQY7SUz6flSyo6SUY2dj_xiaHdGyIhevVs54RaiU-GlCyYKBSwUII6H2mQToA?authuser=0&fife=s16383
https://tjalda.is/en/asbyrgi/
https://parka.is/asbyrgi/
https://www.youtube.com/embed/Rsv940aSL4I

