      <styleUrl>#style_Campsites___Mountain_Huts</styleUrl>
      <Point>
        <coordinates>-16.915147,65.640217,0.0</coordinates>
      </Point>
    </Placemark>
    <Placemark>
      <name>Grimsstadir Guesthouse/Campsite</name>
      <description><![CDATA[North of the Vatnajökull glacier at the crossroads of Route 1 (The Ring Road) and Route864 Dettifoss lies Grímsstaðir farmer´s guesthouse and campground. Big beautiful crystalclear skies and mountain vistas make for a relaxing and peaceful stay. To the south rises Herðubreið the queen of Icelandic mountains. Grímsstaðir is an ideal location for a stay of a few days to relax and enjoy it´s surroundings as well as make day trips to some of the northeast´s natural wonders such as: Dettifoss 28 km Mývatn 40 km Ásbyrgi 56 km km Herðubreiðarlindir 60 km Askja 100 km Kverkfjöll 130 km A big thanks to Sander K. for the following description in 2020: "there is no electricity available, and the facilities are very minimal. Two sheltered outside sinks with only cold running water and one unheated indoor toilet for men and women each. Toilet paper and hand soap was available, but there was no light except for a window. The place looked rather small, with space for maybe 10/15 tents/campers/caravans. On one end the area is bordered by a small river of about 1 meter wide, which you can obviously hear throughout the night. There seems to be a restaurant located in one of the buildings, but that was closed by the time we arrived around 23 at night. We found it perfect for a one night stop and go, especially at that price level. " Phone: +354 464 4292 Price: Kr. 1000/adult Facilities: - WC - Water - Shower - Restaurant (Kr. 1800 for breakfast)

Commentaire: Style: icon:1765,color:E65100

Altitude: 0.0m]]></description>
