    </Placemark>
    <Placemark>
      <name>Flúðir Campsite</name>
      <description><![CDATA[https://tjalda.is/en/fludir/ The town Flúðir has been a popular destination for icelandic tourists as well as foreign tourist mostly because the area is known for good weather. The area has been called “the food chest of Iceland” because of the big growth in vegetables. The camp site has several service buildings with toilets and showers. There is also a washing machine and a tumble dryer. In the camp center (red house at the top of the hill) is a small store selling ice- cream, coals and other camp related products. There are also information brochures on most of the activities offered in south Iceland. In the area there is also wireless internet, big outdoor barbeque, a playground and much more. Running water and electricity is available in most of the camp site. Open: May 15 - Sept 15 Phone: +354 618 5005 Price: Kr. 1750/adult - Kr. 750/10-16 yr. old - FREE for under 10 yr. old Facilities: - WC - Water - Pool/hot tub - Golf course - Electricity (Kr. 1000) - Playground - Hiking paths - Shower - Washer/dryer (Kr. 600/600) - Fishing - Horse rental - Waste disposal - Restaurant - Dogs allowed
https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AKcrxGSHodZn8i9GHwyLBe49YgJJl_5puIuHuGad8YTYXcOboNRCGh6d-dsopzACsm-BkMCjwqEvRVTI1fg7tN2fTwDB009H9qTIynJOgz2wniiGsWpG1-QEr5a_7Srgb6iDj1XfafqNJY9xcVn4MgjT1z0IUaYRU19mvJc_b1ZX0aqfs34ZXrp1FjH3549ofCUpjB3SM6xvyh4Sq5VyI7lWievXOFBQXJ4ZP7g-GDyL1DpAVzSOQ0SQkrYOc18?authuser=0&fife=s16383
https://tjalda.is/en/fludir/

