    </Placemark>
    <Placemark>
      <name>Geysir Campsite</name>
      <description><![CDATA[https://tjalda.is/en/geysir/ The camp site is in a walking distance from the hot springs area, the forest Haukadalsskógur and all the services offered in the area. The service house has showers, toilets, washing facilities, waste disposal and the camp site warden is located there. There is electricity in the upper area but the lower area is meant for tents. It is directly across from the restaurant where they offer fresh fish or meat, selection of soups, pizza, salad, ice cream and much more. There is also a coffe house and a store. At Hotel Geysir is a restaurant with lunch and dinner and a la carte menu. There is a lot to do in the area. The golf course Haukadalsvöllur is close by (www.geysirgolf.is), a horse rental is at the farm Kjóastaðir by Geysir, river rafting and riverjet (http://www.icelandriverjet.is/) as well as salmon fishing in the river Tungufljóti. A great multimedia museum is by the store at Geysir where you can learn a lot about Icelandic nature. You can feel the power in Icelandic nature and learn about volcanic eruptions, avalanches, earthquakes, northern lights and ice caves. Open:1 June - 1 September Phone: +354 480 6800 Price: Kr. 1800/adult - Kr. 500/8-15 yr. - Free for 7 and younger Facilities: - WC - Water - Shower (Kr. 500) - Electricity (Kr. 1000) - Restaurant - Golf course - Playground - WiFi - Hiking paths - Washer/dryer - Waste disposal - Horse rental
https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AKcrxGSxP1SjI7q6I5xFDPM5-yXsJ-fNfdAXhgqlOABnChsix5wRpJui4dH-ql41awpB__f3nROEx9uOh_dgz58BObN9DYglyaMH0Yo9T3LapnkwoxlSztk_lD-2h9HqC6z8E9PKmwF187TR6KpgX4G1KZO8iwRHt-ul_Lxjq85-K2Qrxu3zZo1DlR78sLhlMHfOkB82lhQkjw-7cVKi3APjwOFczJnyoyG8Ic_wJwZTXJ9Z5ICMQoDt51jy4JY?authuser=0&fife=s16383
