    </Placemark>
    <Placemark>
      <name>Þjórsárver Campsite</name>
      <description><![CDATA[Þjórsárver is located at Villingaholt close to the river Þjórsá. The river runs by the eastern side of the area and is very well visable from the camp site. The river has broken a lot of land during the time and some farms have been moved from the river. The view from Þjórsárver is beautiful with many mountains in the horizon. When the visibility is good you can see many mountains such as the volcanos Eyjafjallajökull and Hekla, Skálafell, Búrfell and Kálfstinda to name a few. You can also see out to the Vestmanislands. To the west of Þjórsárver is a small lake called Villingaholtsvatn. The camp site has toilets and showers. There is a washing machine automat also. An excellent playground for children. The Tourist sercive Vatnsholt www.hotelvatnsholt.is is close by where there is a restaurant, horse rental, boat rental and a small zoo. Phone: +354 899 7748 Price: Kr. 1500/adult - Kr. Facilities: - WC - Water - Shower - Washing machine (Kr. 300) - Electricity (Kr. 1000) - Restaurant - Playground - Fishing - Bike rental - Horse rental

Commentaire: Style: icon:1765,color:000000

Altitude: 0.0m]]></description>
      <styleUrl>#style_Campsites___Mountain_Huts</styleUrl>
      <Point>
        <coordinates>-20.7545,63.880783,0.0</coordinates>
      </Point>
    </Placemark>
    <Placemark>
      <name>Stokkseyri Campsite</name>
      <description><![CDATA[https://tjalda.is/en/stokkseyri/ Stokkseyri is a small village known for its wild bird life and breathtaking waterfront where coastal sand, rapids and lakes can be found. The village is famous for its art and cultural life with studios from various artists, and a few galleries with handcrafted items. At Stokkseyri you will find a hunting museum, a pipe organ workshop, the Ghost museum as well as the Elf-, Trolls and Northern light museum. Lobster restaurant called Fjöruborðið with famous lobster meal and soup, lovely coffee house called KaffiGott and the gas station serves pizzas and burgers, among other necessaries. The swimming pool at Stokkseyri is small and cozy with hot tubs as well as a children’s pool. The camp site has recently been renovated with new toilet facilities, showers, a washing machine and plenty of electric poles. The camp site has a play area for the children and there is a walking path from the camp site to the center of the village. Phone: +354 896 2144 Price: Kr. 1500/adult (Free for 12 and younger) Facilities: - WC - Water (cold) - Cooking facilities - Shower (Kr. 200) - Electricity (Kr. 1000) - Playground - Hiking path - Pool/hot tub - Waste disposal - Restaurant
https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AKcrxGRQN3k-LXv-KK1cPko6mG7S2zZFwIV699pnKqMKbJ81AvhwSMIFSphbmqDHzWdjhBUH14tI_s7w_XmKWjZE4_E8iM-Hv1lOVGt6A2WlXHteErW8ZPmSWgBHyh00MBwL4Qrmg_ftDDHdXje_yXOTUacFNtbqo1T2MfA3jLhqtGGxdHffJW1s8SptRIPa08retSUdqouxkfavn8THTrUsHoPawbBMJgz5lN24F7ce8dvagsJu10swlr1MtqY?authuser=0&fife=s16383
