    <Placemark>
      <name>Laugaland Campsite</name>
      <description><![CDATA[https://goo.gl/maps/QsPJot7xtdZNgX9M7 The camp site is sheltered and good family camp site. It should be quiet around midnight. Recently the camp site was extended and it is now divided in two areas. There are excellent facilities for children such as two football fields, three playground and one with a monkey swing and trampoline. The swimming pool has hot tubs, a water slide and a steambath. The opening time is from 10:00 – 19:00 during the weekend and 14:00 – 22:00 during the weekdays. The camp sita has an outdoor barbeque, waste disposal, electricity and much more. Dogs are allowed at Laugaland provided that they are kept in a leash and of course that the owners clean up after them. The surroundings at Laugaland are beautiful and it is ideal to go on walks around the area. There is a marked path from Laugalandi to the forestry field in the area. It is good to take a picnic bag with on that walk ans use the outdoor tables in the forest. The walk there and back is about 5 km long. The church area Marteinstunga is in about 1,5 km walking distance from Laugaland. The horse ranch is also in walking distance (4 km) where you can see old saddlery, see videos about the Icelandic horse, pet and comb the horses and the children can try to go horseback riding under supervision. Open: May 15 - September 15 Phone: +354 895 6543 Price: Kr. 1600/adult (Free for 17 and younger) Facilities: - WC - Water - Electricity (Kr. 1000) - Playground - Hiking paths - Pool/hot tub - Waste disposal - Dogs allowed
https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AKcrxGQ90X5aigNwGO65cKdUkIFHv-c2h2DUwW7X5EOq7sDQ-Lj9GrpyrNlOI4RRc_uKEKUxTBX4KMnWH_s0XLdHctauGS5Kf5ALzpbn1F_8ZKbgZH-K_KXqj4OOFjHm1CkkTiPuOcCGmI25H8OkrwT9oUMup5lmALtcVQyH5YRumrGp_FoC24zVJ0PB-lM2i4mb0H1Pzd1RIy-zXla2McgrwVKHQ1KzvRENLIrUctQks_9JOMZeJhRwkBQ1GXg?authuser=0&fife=s16383
https://goo.gl/maps/QsPJot7xtdZNgX9M7

