      <Point>
        <coordinates>-22.038724,65.679227,0.0</coordinates>
      </Point>
    </Placemark>
    <Placemark>
      <name>Laugafell</name>
      <description><![CDATA[MOUNTAIN HUT CAMPSITE Like all mountain hut campsites, it is very remote and has limited facilities and is not recommended for campervan travelers. Laugafell hut is located on the high plateau of North Icleand, 15 km NE of Hofsjökull glacier and 20 km SW from the end of Eyjafjarðardalur valley. The old hut was built in 1948-50 and the sanitary house with sleeping accommodation was built in 1994-98. The accommodation in the huts is a sleeping bag accommodation. Guests must bring their own sleeping bags. The old hut sleeps 20 and the sleeping loft in the sanitary house sleeps 12. The houses are heated all year round with geothermally hot water. There is gas for cooking. The sanitary house has WC facilities and changing cubicles for the adjacent swimming pool. The camping place is beside the huts. There is a warden at Laugafell in July, August and the beginning of September. The huts are locked in the winter but the toilets and changing facilities are open all year round. The Laugafell area is conveniently located for 4-wheel drive traffic on the northern high ground of Iceland as tracks lead from Laugafell to Eyjafjörður (F821), Skagafjörður (F752), Bárðardalur (F881 and F26) and the South via Sprengisandur (F752 and F26). Phone number (in summer): (+354-) 833-5697. Price: N/A e-mail: ffa@ffa.is phone number: +354 462 2720

Commentaire: Style: icon:1603,color:000000

Altitude: 0.0m]]></description>
      <styleUrl>#style_Campsites___Mountain_Huts</styleUrl>
      <Point>
        <coordinates>-18.331627,65.027717,0.0</coordinates>
      </Point>
    </Placemark>
    <Placemark>
      <name>Skælingar</name>
      <description><![CDATA[https://goo.gl/maps/bqnDRAtN1Avfpm9h9 MOUNTAIN HUT CAMPSITE Like most mountain hut campsites, this campsite is very remote and difficult to get to and is therefore not recommended for campervan travelers. This is a restored a decayed farmers’ sheep roundup shelter in 1996-97. Its surroundings are breathtakingly beautiful. Large lava outcrops and the vegetation remind of a park. A short walk takes you to Holaskjol, but one day’s hikes include Mt Uxatindar and Mt Gjatindur. A rather difficult 4wd track continues to the hut from the track to Mt Gjatindur. The hut offers mattresses and a gas-stove, but no other utensils. It is heated with oil, but is not insulated, and therefore not meant for winter use. It houses 16 persons. June 20 - August 31 Price: Kr. 2500/person Telephone: +354 562 1000 utivist@utivist.is
https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AKcrxGRnOKnobAiN82Re91vAJV9ND1ds0Zr2Sz1qOTCE0FhiRwA6Mh-aJA-k3cdspRCrTh4r8PwtG5Xlz7FATZ6-73tc0Nl0ZIulkpveZVIiZKfoHP_sd2_FU8yX1WvAq5CXeIgEYU6BdQ6qnRll6E-bYfrb--477q2Y93mcNinYAekp-sjwBn24s77mlE7wndTx9gjx3JF7FASf6o0qD2oHiSbCDq2STHIVMs32WlTohkZaSPU2vWW8qxAdBto?authuser=0&fife=s16383
