    <Placemark>
      <name>Laxness museum</name>
      <description><![CDATA[https://goo.gl/maps/nLwE5EiDmVkzx9J9A Halldór Laxnes Museum. Halldór Laxness (1902-1998) stands head and shoulders above the other Icelandic writers of the 20th century. He was prolific during his long career, writing 13 major novels, five plays and a dramatisation of one of his novels, not to mention his collections of short stories, essays and memoirs. His books have been translated into 43 languages and published in more than 500 editions. His career was unique, the diversity of his works almost without parallel, and with every book he can be said to have approached his readers from a new and unexpected direction.
https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AKcrxGTyl3xzZIVV3GJk2ohqdVUWkmggIagAfg8Sc8eNB29742PaQ2F7r-hRXCD20ghibcw1_xEDa4VK4I2ijMMT0K3pEwHS-ITyyvY7JA55EGZrr-L4EjDc-XUjoECuBvJo2NV8vI-wkRVb4N2voTaeDg0mEdvwoP4ZJ3Bz1zTdj7iTKaYoSwI4fGOeRimXLjJnoB-G7lXXKop6YjbIvIi7yNrZBk25kDKxHtF70Ga_mmt899VHPWl9zK-zUhs?authuser=0&fife=s16383
