    <Placemark>
      <name>The Thórbergur museum</name>
      <description><![CDATA[https://goo.gl/maps/rPsnAsbH3X9BDkzh6 Cultural heritage museum, restaurant and walking trails in the South East of Iceland. The Þórbergur center is a cultural center with an exhibition dedicated to the great writer Þórbergur Þórðarson (1888 – 1974) ) who grew up on the farm Hali, situated on the ring road near Jökulsárlón, the famous iceberg lagoon in the South East of Iceland.
