    <Placemark>
      <name>The Húsavík Whale Museum</name>
      <description><![CDATA[https://goo.gl/maps/vHCVC813EQyQSsV9A The Whale Museum, formerly called Whale Centre, began as a trial, with a small exhibition on whales. Only three years after its establishment, the popularity of the exhibit made it necessary to acquire a bigger building. What had once been an abandoned slaughterhouse in town is now one of the most visited places in the north of Iceland, providing 1.600m2 to display whale skeletons of several species and fascinating facts about the whales.
https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AKcrxGSweZqKIhF3yDwMTa3mPQbixtSbbQXqYYjdTfj7sxxj7iMtqjnvPiBpjWw9BxCyQHYldtYQPQkhwjwGCA08r1LUr4VK8nOPSLqymgJrRvqkrf7UdMtnOoM-O-2pkwDptk1s5Dxfw3jbpkeb6PjBSrIUjNg9ctxx3_az7kZcE84o_Ah6zAlcBtxV9ec9Nf5HXJVtcyotoM1WStzb4IQXhEF5U7yiDB7e2cYkDU4msIQXtu8RM7g0bZz74tk?authuser=0&fife=s16383
