    <Placemark>
      <name>Arctic Fox museum</name>
      <description><![CDATA[https://goo.gl/maps/6Qix2ovJHyEGvKraA The Arctic Fox Centre is a non-profit research and exhibition center, focusing on the arctic fox (Vulpes lagopus) - the only native terrestrial mammal in Iceland. The Arctic Fox Centre was established on September 15th 2007 in Sudavik Westfjords. Founders were 42, mostly local people, tourist operators and municipalities in the Westfjords. All of which share their interest in the arctic foxes and believe in increasing ecotourism in Iceland. The idea of the Arctic Fox Centre comes from prof. Pall Hersteinsson, University of Iceland and he serves as a quality witness for the center.
https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AKcrxGQLdP4r-GlaMR1Kju8J7xaOKMBeJAn_cdOqCz1Qk_EFVM6Eqxdoe4wDmoWVZvMKkM95rdeDUolclNGuln-g7TRopOKkYg6Jwq3da6X3_Hk7bxN7AsQGSbCIUdUY--Uvy_eWh56BVfo5y15DkL3iwu7y535xXCjFFwbBRy9Nq4aERI_Pd067tBIm3ATtD8grcFTtC4BUC2rqaTu1zyHiNi6MV09BBzqjCxnJjgOxGxTrSddjgGRE-nOljOE?authuser=0&fife=s16383
