    <Placemark>
      <name>Puffins Vestmannaeyjar</name>
      <description><![CDATA[https://goo.gl/maps/FTg8YP4B1Ttx6Prv6 The volcanic archipelago of islands just off the south coast, the Westman Islands are a hive of puffin activity. Heimaey is home to the world's largest puffin colony, it's towering volcanic cliffs providing the perfect place for the little birds to make their nests. The island is accessed via a ferry or plane.
