    <Placemark>
      <name>Puffins Látrabjarg</name>
      <description><![CDATA[https://goo.gl/maps/Nqn2VET6RsBBHFdi8 The westernmost point of Iceland, Latrabjarg cliffs are widely considered one of the best bird watching spots in all of Europe. 14km of cliffs stretch along the peninsula, and you can get up close and personal with the puffins by crawling carefully towards the edge of the cliff.
