    <Placemark>
      <name>Puffins Hornstrandir Nature Reserve</name>
      <description><![CDATA[More at https://epiciceland.net/hornstrandir-guide/ The most remote location in all of Iceland, the uninhabited Hornstrandir was a hideout for bandits and outlaws. Nowadays, it's a beautiful location for hiking in the wilderness and spotting puffins on the cliffs. There are no services here, so you must take all that you need for at least a couple of days with you on your back.
https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AKcrxGTRuHmTapLPASysMnDDcYnQDguRAEwwlYhUn5hX57EsNU0nKRYTaqzJC5SwVgsORexr5zAVSGLrENltX0fXZ2R9IB1BV_khlVY_qrfynJwC_XITiHgS6GQfCP1hQyydOpyyiUc7VBSWcq2n2rWpHzhUDczAcXQr9c1j2Ki-WMNeCL3o44pKIA0s4BkSgyPxal7AcdYEpLSKDE1iI9P2zyp2CtTHtLV2EmQEjIYn_KV1uMbHJn1o4oK65lI?authuser=0&fife=s16383
