    <Placemark>
      <name>Solheimajokull Glacier view</name>
      <description><![CDATA[https://epiciceland.net/best-winter-tours-iceland/#21_Solheimajokull_glacier_hike Solheimajokull is a glacier snout which is part of the larger Myrdalsjokull (1480m) -- the fourth largest glacier in Iceland. New paved road lead to the glacier visitor center and there is a small cafe with wifi here. You can walk to the glacier in minutes. Good to get close to the glacier if you don't plan to do glacier walk. Note that the glacier is covered in ash from recent volcanic activities thus the black color. It's a beautiful spot worth stopping for sure
https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AKcrxGTjDJkRfS79DfN4sHq_yNWbg2k_VqrFkBiNv4ZB1JzdrlH6MddGc_5vEyULQA1iZqz8PX7pddVCmpzCxd77y4y616lNgFUNEyKej8-UG7UQIBKKtJjmOIybTqk3KkPpWqH1kcCOwoIP1RrJ73NN7U47nxkG0JfQ34QoNUjd_vdQqXSjXfzrLvsy6EEIUxXIaOQc3fefi-gI35S3knZXErIekrno0283jPn6I3YlUkjZP8GZ91OXnJmcuNw?authuser=0&fife=s16383
