    <Placemark>
      <name>Búða beach</name>
      <description><![CDATA[https://goo.gl/maps/LiZ2yYZdB7aV91z29 Small beach unknown to most tourists. It is small and very beautiful, with golden sand contrasts with the deep black of the volcanic rocks scattered like "topping." There was hardly anyone. To access it, you must leave your vehicle in the parking lot of the church and surround the walk up to the cemetery behind. From there out several roads and right to reach the beach "secret" is what he left. The other paths do not follow in spring already carried Kría nests (S. Paradisaea) some birds very protective and will not hesitate to attack you in order to get out of where their offspring.
