    <Placemark>
      <name>Selárdalur</name>
      <description><![CDATA[https://goo.gl/maps/6StPBz95GU51a8dT6 If you want something totally different take the road past Bíldudalur to Selárdalur which is an isolated farm house with completely odd sculptures an eccentric artist built at his house (which have since been restored). It's a bit odd/random, and the drive is one of the most spectacular i've done. And on top of that on the drive you drive right past 2 gold sand beaches
https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AKcrxGRjxjmUmznbKkVka4ze4De3Bu2P3Zrij-v7m9HloO2MA4pnVsPQACOxhHadsmMwUgnPxdCJH8D1R4Wc_d_YvD1vel5GIraODVC_kcpyfVTtGAG-uGCiMgTKV3tAxpXTDqLfD-dwyjJFfTe9Nf3cmaSo5WXXaZrzBw6BbL-TYs5fmqLEsluCsBNHifjZdEe7_FrK5JnzwLR3jZCfLSzdbbMrCwO0pbZfg8QerLxEORarHeUq4qQZOBTnGVs?authuser=0&fife=s16383
https://goo.gl/maps/6StPBz95GU51a8dT6

