    <Placemark>
      <name>Skalavik</name>
      <description><![CDATA[https://www.westfjords.is/en/place/skalavik Skálavík is the next creek westwards from Bolungarvík. People lived in Skálavík until around 1960's and since then the creek has been uninhabited. People from the area and people who have relations to Skálavík have restored some of the houses and new summerhouses have been built. In a good summer day the people from the area like to build sandcastles on the beach, take a walk and even swim in the river. Skálavík is a paradise for kids and a perfect place to stop the car and play around. On the way from Skálavík, we recommend driving all the way up to the top of the moutain and take a look at the view from the top.
https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AKcrxGTiUUZDHRQFw10aCjI3NxFy24gWPe3ze9zFaamuL2FeAd3OrBwcEAsZs9RkRqDmEK-R4avKrfy3g9gHHuTAAKUxyeoJl7eXcQvoyXvp-GDZn66JTLANLdA5f7bdLT7Y7GoyMMGO3tuMOh1EYJR5Aw52imGDIA4xk79NuC5uvAK21Kf7gueXmtj2iAOeYZwK4L_nKdQB9cmwWIWvCc9KSff6sh0WOFZacZ_uKeJ5_czST1mTirs0mPr_ZJQ?authuser=0&fife=s16383
https://www.westfjords.is/en/place/skalavik

