    <Placemark>
      <name>Kaldalon Trail</name>
      <description><![CDATA[https://goo.gl/maps/3zELp71ThmerAy4j8 Kaldalón is a beautiful fjord (or lake ?) and you can walk to Drangajökull glacier from there or possibly drive 4WD to get closer to the glacier. Here's directions: At the deepest part of Kaldalón, near the bridge, is a track in the direction of the glacier. Just before a small hill, it splits. Take the right branch and go around the hill. You can drive for another km before you end at a sort of parking. This is the start of the hike. IMO it's safe, and not too difficult (mostly flat). The full hike (both ways) took me about 2,5 hours. The first part of the hike is on small hills. It's is not marked, but there are tracks that you can follow. The second part is across grassland which can be rather swampy. You als have to jump over several streams. The last part is a rocky sand plain that becomes a big field of stones when close to the glacier. You also have to cross a small glacial river. You can walk to the foot of the glacier, but I would not recomment hiking up. https://www.wikiloc.com/hiking-trails/kaldalon-18809422#direcctions
https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AKcrxGSdpcAy_c97hJSwqVVOBgMU0gHtJYHU-NLx9lmvrupwgi7jKfiuh9NMjDNMuyurM3X8oah3qMnmU_0k-pP1z0ijU55tgiWZkr4UnWCRvHW71WkWFmIqMee1tcc4d_QNqhUQ0PJ5TOR9gx5mQKghYf53lU-MUi-MydU4n88juxPBXbTnhPZXBvMfbPErrpCyiHyJ4EmefrNM8Fk9zuOGW4bN_5agoP39KMJSivg3-ab8S1mjxE98tANs5kA?authuser=0&fife=s16383
https://goo.gl/maps/3zELp71ThmerAy4j8
https://www.wikiloc.com/hiking-trails/kaldalon-18809422#direcctions

