    <Placemark>
      <name>Kaldbakur</name>
      <description><![CDATA[https://goo.gl/maps/2qHvJ8gpG3TmGACu5 Reachable by hiking or mountain biking! Kaldbakur is one of the so-called Westfjords Alps - the tall and pointy mountain range between Dýrafjörður and Arnarfjörður. Most Westfjords mountains are flat topped as a result of Ice Age glaciers, but the "Alps" are tall and pointy and look a little bit like, well, the Alps…Kaldbakur is the tallest of them and, at 998 metres tall, it is the tallest mountain in the Westfjords region.
https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AKcrxGSUkAua0SWqdWNalMpXlVHviIp33epV2A4E-ZI_C74UzazEzf6v7XFWGrGc7yMWc-XQj8W-mGwgunhX_WRdTjDld7lTVLqBfL4nukcoGOEXH8hlM-9Ywnyl-8a2DAksC4n7tDybQJ5QIWHntRpEASrFOXpeM-gR9GxMhScpsTohWSxDbeKRPA4fggfpneCNC1CkEbi_hRu-a7iuXExZp3q29ocRtqQTBlmFwDvlSYoersSbiKumI4JaNGE?authuser=0&fife=s16383
