    <Placemark>
      <name>Ytri Tunga</name>
      <description><![CDATA[https://goo.gl/maps/txKGqbAUTgGpPUvk7 Ytri-Tunga is a very popular beach for seal-spotting as a seal-colony resides here, as it were. The primary season for seal-spotting is in June and July, but I have seen the seals in the winter months as well. You can see both the common seal and the grey seal at Ytri-Tunga, but the grey seal is bigger than the common seal. The seals you will see on top of rocks or on the beach are usually the common seals. On the information sign below, which is by the parking lot at Ytri-Tunga, you will see the difference between these 2 seals, the one to the left is the common seal and the one to the right is the grey seal.
https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AKcrxGSgA_16emtpN7ch59cPEKhVskMStFF3jjcKYW1rp0SyMtTivlBca6zboFg0Yrf8vzEGD8LD3ZLEpgLtobP_x9TEVC25X0vR_ubpmem3IDens8fCwMic4pXOFxuT8nZupeoLdUUO6hK3lSkmVQsipcNxImz7pXUE_Zj1oPAvKGZtzMa2o8-stkMazPcwh3ctUBb80WTjl-n0rPufVypwcXgYQbZp0E7JP71-K2Zn_cBYfZYkSNlHWzE6cT0?authuser=0&fife=s16383
