    <Placemark>
      <name>Stuðlagil Canyon (West)</name>
      <description><![CDATA[https://epiciceland.net/day-6-askja-studlagil-canyon/#Studlagil_canyon_western_side_eastern_side https://goo.gl/maps/hErYYRnP79WgJT2r8 Although the natural wonder Stuðlagil and the basalt columns have always been here, much of this fascinating landscape was underwater level in the forceful river Jökla only recently. It is almost hard to believe when standing by the picturesque, relaxing river watching the birds swim in joy and harmony that this was a terrifying place under the forceful pressure of a dominating and angry river. It is by any standard one of the most beautiful place in Iceland where you can see and photograph exceptional basalt columns. This location is for accessing the viewing platform on the west side, you cannot descend down to the river. Good if you are short on time. As of July 2021, there is a food truck and a WC (need to pay). It's much better to visit this place early or mid summer if possible. the river in Stuðlagil canyon actually changes colour late in the summer. It is blue/green until august, when the dam at Kárahnjúkar releases surplus water from the reservoir into the river which in turn colors it murky brown.
https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AKcrxGTrlvV5FPErpkiGZOefyxlEKGdB48q2GE2siCmFmdGIsVgVz-UgBWnqY5zBca2J76bb148h8zzW3DfRQG8oOqzrUAYWa8ybBoP4XWX8GlRdUl3cbr1m_qZ2etYLgQVb1KfDKBqrku-FeaWjJIS7X2_fHvt5tR8_cON0ILxI69QchBIxFEKMOlZ2GQita4fl0uizRpNmk7C7xdgEC250dQye885n_l6Uunk5h1ZGFjDVZiO2ox-ZSsdwkUw?authuser=0&fife=s16383
https://epiciceland.net/day-6-askja-studlagil-canyon/#Studlagil_canyon_western_side_eastern_side
https://goo.gl/maps/hErYYRnP79WgJT2r8

