    <Placemark>
      <name>Studlagil Canyon (East)</name>
      <description><![CDATA[https://goo.gl/maps/ev9bSKS2egD86F1a8 This is a parking lot where you can hike (~ 4km roundtrip) to the bottom of the canyon. IMO, this is much better vantage point than the west side. Allow 2-3 hours here. Important note: the river in Stuðlagil canyon actually changes colour late in the summer. It is blue/green until august, when the dam at Kárahnjúkar releases surplus water from the reservoir into the river which in turn colors it murky brown. So it´s always better to visit this place early or mid summer if possible.
