    <Placemark>
      <name>Karlinn</name>
      <description><![CDATA[https://goo.gl/maps/KyDUZcJWVDcgCXEw9 Karlinn („The Man“) is a 50-60 m high seacliff, an eroded volcanic plug, which stands high and mighty just off the coast of Valahnúkur. Karlinn is popular spot with visitors and especially among photographers, as it is truly picturesque when the unremitting waves hit the rock.
