    <Placemark>
      <name>Kárahnjúkavirkjun</name>
      <description><![CDATA[https://goo.gl/maps/4baCJiNNfZEJ3dB18 The Power Plant at Kárahnjúkar is the largest construction project in Icelandic history and the most significant electricity production in the country. The Kárahnjúkar Power Plant was built to produce energy for the aluminum plant at Reyðarfjörður. A trip to Kárahnjúkar is an ideal road trip for the family. A paved road runs from Fljótsdalur to the Kárahnjúkar dam. The Kárahnjúkar area is ideal for outdoor activities. It is fun to see the Kárahnjúkar Dam itself and the Hálslón Reservoir. When Hálslón fills up and overflows, the Hverfandi waterfall appears at the western end of the dam, where the water plunges about 100 meters into Hafrahvammahljúfur. The waterfall is mighty and can become more powerful than Dettifoss. There are also fun hiking trails in the area; for example, there is a great hiking trail along Hafrahvammagljúfur and to Magnahellir, but to get to the starting point of the marked hiking trail, you need a four-wheel-drive car.
https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AKcrxGQryorEskktHFkZZIyn1PkHSunkv1IhTMDeEwCkqGTs7WG4zyW0AfrqIn43rBu1hRtOIz0Y28pzBWauQmo3FU7OQG2nlA-NKLcBVYkx86ebYfoiDiCs_dy61R58JD6GTNLIDv9UEnExjd_QLTN7pYKhsnZpTIFLCk-yYGIFNVjv7lfpKpdXLgcUIqREHLUPn5k1ggCft2ye14NJdH85Ufqy8UjfNxY_fnkdKCBsDh7BHGOdGcC1Kp71qlc?authuser=0&fife=s16383
https://goo.gl/maps/4baCJiNNfZEJ3dB18

Commentaire: Style: icon:1574,color:FF5252 | gx_media_links: https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AKcrxGQryorEskktHFkZZIyn1PkHSunkv1IhTMDeEwCkqGTs7WG4zyW0AfrqIn43rBu1hRtOIz0Y28pzBWauQmo3FU7OQG2nlA-NKLcBVYkx86ebYfoiDiCs_dy61R58JD6GTNLIDv9UEnExjd_QLTN7pYKhsnZpTIFLCk-yYGIFNVjv7lfpKpdXLgcUIqREHLUPn5k1ggCft2ye14NJdH85Ufqy8UjfNxY_fnkdKCBsDh7BHGOdGcC1Kp71qlc?authuser=0&fife=s16383

