    <Placemark>
      <name>Raudinupur Cape</name>
      <description><![CDATA[https://goo.gl/maps/aNMDAb9N8FoxHXDf9 Amazing cliff to watch tons of birds! " Almost on the northern tip of Iceland. Possibly it is the place where more birds I have been able to see, even puffins, it is a big cliff right next to the lighthouse. You have to walk on a road full of huge stones, which It is not very easy to walk by. Once you get there you will see all kinds of birds. You have to be very careful with the nests of the puffins, they are very close to the cliffs and the caves where they nest are very fragile. They usually nest there from June to August, and the nest is for life for the couple, each year they have the same nest from generation to generation. You will see them flying over their nests with the fish in their beaks. It was a very satisfying experience."
https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AKcrxGQ7HQIksFNFpoSKhJLlwoicdWNB_jPIZq0POjbsDSY_-QSB631aWRqyeDtey-6CbaiIB4Rx17Eo83QhRym_YylCJsHjhqI1MA6y78Pf1M9XA8jq6XYd_bWTe1bAUmIxrN5XjLgJEyRHDfFS9BMuVTwP33TwuZzRyDxselB6TqyqCfQV4FXsgRDmGMTEkPEaprgcKSqRiNT-j5QHAX8KeLiwEIVacTZIo8sPNzyDAavjrSSFu_jO4MTYgBM?authuser=0&fife=s16383
