    <Placemark>
      <name>Filming Location: Jökulsárlón</name>
      <description><![CDATA[James Bond - A View to a Kill (1985) The opening scene of the film takes place in Siberia and was filmed in Switzerland and Iceland. At the end of the scene, James Bond (Roger Moore) is being chased by a helicopter on the lagoon. He shoots the helicopter down which explodes on an iceberg. Bond then hides in a submarine that is made to look like an iceberg in the lagoon. Filming on the lagoon was quite risky because the crew and actors had to climb icebergs that could collapse at any moment. Roger Moore did not come to Iceland, but a double was used. James Bond - Die Another Day (2002) Gustav Graves (Toby Stephens) owns a diamond mine in Iceland and James Bond (Pierce Brosnan) goes to Iceland to investigate Graves' mysterious behavior. At Jökulsárlón is Graves' ice hotel as well as a race between him and Bond. The scenes are a combination of shots at Jökulsárlón, computer generated scenes and studio shots. In order for the lake to freeze, a dam was built at the end of the lake to prevent seawater from mixing with it.

Commentaire: Style: icon:1709,color:006064

Altitude: 0.0m]]></description>
      <styleUrl>#style_Attractions</styleUrl>
      <Point>
        <coordinates>-16.1759299,64.0596609,0.0</coordinates>
      </Point>
    </Placemark>
